      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;144-phase-4-display-searched-places-on-map&#34;&gt;14.4. Phase 4: Display Searched Places on Map&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#144-phase-4-display-searched-places-on-map&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The last part of our app is to show a place selected from the search results on the map and navigate to it.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The task seems complicated, but we already have the code to display the annotations for a place, right? The rest of it is pretty straightforward.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Let&amp;rsquo;s open ViewController.swift file and add a method &lt;code&gt;showSelectedPlace(placeItem: MKMapItem)&lt;/code&gt; there:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;{% code lineNumbers=&amp;ldquo;true&amp;rdquo; %}&lt;/p&gt;</description>
